# For linux users

    -> Open your terminal amd write this: <-
    =====================================
        cd ~/smart-ids
        source .venv/bin/activate
        sudo .venv/bin/python ui.py
    =====================================


    -> ICPM Detection (LOW severity ICMP events and counter increases) <-
    ======================================
    ping -c 5 8.8.8.8
    ======================================

    -> Suspicious Port Test <-
    ======================================
    nc -zv 192.168.10.9 23
    or  telnet 192.168.10.9 23
    ======================================


    -> Port Scan Test (Realisitic Attack Simulation) <-
    ======================================
    nmap -Pn -p 1-100 192.168.10.9
    ======================================
    ->/ Mutilple ports accessed
    ->/ could trigger MEDIUM or HIGH
    ->/ Port scan counter increases
    ->/ add -Pn because i forced it to just scan ports not just do host discovery
    ======================================


    -> SYN Scan (Advanced) <-
    ======================================
    sudo nmap -sS 192.168.10.9
    ======================================
    ->/ This is a half open scan. It should trigger after threshold reached
    =======================================================================


    -> Normal Traffic (False Positive Test)
    =======================================
    curl https://google.com or any other sites
    ==========================================

# For window users

    -> 1. ICMP Detection (LOW severity) <-
    ======================================
    ping -n 5 8.8.8.8
    ======================================

    -> 2. Suspicious Port Test <-
    ======================================
    Test-NetConnection -ComputerName 192.168.10.9 -Port 23
    ======================================
    ->/ Triggers MEDIUM severity alert
    ->/ Logs specific suspicious port access

    -> 3. Port Scan Test (Realistic Attack Simulation) <-
    ======================================
    nmap -Pn -p 1-100 192.168.10.9
    ======================================
    ->/ Note: You must have Nmap installed on Windows for this to work.
    ->/ Multiple ports accessed could trigger MEDIUM or HIGH

    -> 4. SYN Scan (Advanced) <-
    ======================================
    nmap -sS 192.168.10.9
    ======================================
    ->/ Note: Removed 'sudo'. PowerShell must be running as Administrator.
    ->/ This is a half-open scan. It should trigger HIGH severity.
